+//                    127.0.0.1, AF_INET, not AF_UNIX -- so both ends are
+//                    ordinary sockets poll() will wait on. It works, and it
+//                    made every Dart timer on this port fire at 5 Hz.
+//
+//                    **Loopback delivery on this console runs on a ~200 ms
+//                    tick.** Measured six ways in spikes/t1-timers: a byte
+//                    written to a socketpair reaches a waiting reader ~197 ms
+//                    after the wait began, wherever in that window the write
+//                    lands, and it makes no difference whether the reader is in
+//                    poll(), in a blocking recv(), in sceNetRecv() on a raw
+//                    sceNet socket, or in sceNetEpollWait(). It is not poll and
+//                    it is not epoll; it is the loopback interface. Timeouts,
+//                    by contrast, are exact to a tenth of a millisecond in all
+//                    four.
